</div></div><div  class="perc-region perc-noAutoResize perc-fixed perc-vertical entry group "  data-noautoresize="false" id="temp-region-12"> <div class=" perc-vertical "><div  class="perc-region perc-region-leaf perc-noAutoResize perc-fixed perc-vertical "  data-noautoresize="false" id="region-title"> <div class=" perc-vertical ">        <div class="perc-widget" >

        
<div>

<h1>2026 General Election</h1>
</div>
    
    
</div>
</div></div><div  class="perc-region perc-region-leaf perc-noAutoResize perc-fixed perc-vertical "  data-noautoresize="false" id="region-facility"> <div class=" perc-vertical "></div></div><div  class="perc-region perc-region-leaf perc-noAutoResize perc-fixed perc-vertical "  data-noautoresize="false" id="region-body"> <div class=" perc-vertical ">        <div class="perc-widget" >
<div>

<div class="rxbodyfield"><h2><strong>General Election is Nov. 3, 2026</strong></h2><p>The 2026 New Hampshire General Election will be held on Tuesday, Nov. 3, 2026. Polls will be open from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m. </p><h2>COAST to offer free rides to the polls on Election Day</h2><p>COAST will offer free rides to anyone on their way to vote in the Elections on Tuesday, Nov. 3. While the COAST public transit system does not provide transportation to each individual polling station directly, COAST said the goal is to encourage voters to get to the polls and participate in voting by eliminating the barrier of transportation costs.</p><p>All passengers need to do is tell their driver that they are on their way to vote, or on the way back from voting, and they will not be charged for the ride. COAST will be following an honor system.</p><p>For more information, visit <a href="https://coastbus.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">coastbus.org</a></p><div class="rxbodyfield"><h2><a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?themes&amp;themes=%5B%22wards-and-polling-places%22%5D" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><img alt="" data-jcrpath="//2025.03.06_wardmap.png" data-pathitem="{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;16777215-101-43455&quot;,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;ASSET&quot;,&quot;folderPaths&quot;:&quot;//Folders/$System$/Assets/government/open-government/img&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;2025.03.06_wardmap.png&quot;,&quot;revisionable&quot;:true,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;percImageAsset&quot;,&quot;leaf&quot;:true,&quot;hasItemChildren&quot;:false,&quot;hasFolderChildren&quot;:false,&quot;hasSectionChildren&quot;:false,&quot;mobilePreviewEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;accessLevel&quot;:&quot;ADMIN&quot;,&quot;columnData&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;typeProperties&quot;:{&quot;entries&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}" height="328" src="/Assets/government/open-government/img/2025.03.06_wardmap.png" style="float: right;" title="Ward Map Image 2025" width="250"/></a>City of Dover polling locations</h2><p>Dover has the following six polling places:</p><p>Ward 1 - <a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?abuttersDistance=200&amp;latlng=43.208305%2C-70.884092&amp;panel=themes&amp;previewId=36030-000000&amp;themes=%22%5B%5C%22wards-and-polling-places%5C%22%5D%22&amp;zoom=13" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Frances G. Hopkins Elementary School, 78 Horne St.</a><br/>Ward 2 - <a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?abuttersDistance=200&amp;latlng=43.195861%2C-70.87595&amp;panel=themes&amp;previewId=26002-000000&amp;themes=%22%5B%5C%22wards-and-polling-places%5C%22%5D%22&amp;zoom=13" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Dover Ice Arena, 110 Portland Ave.</a><br/>Ward 3 - <a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?abuttersDistance=200&amp;latlng=43.189983%2C-70.881764&amp;panel=themes&amp;previewId=13004-000000&amp;themes=%22%5B%5C%22wards-and-polling-places%5C%22%5D%22&amp;zoom=13" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Woodman Park Elementary School, 11 Towle Ave.</a><br/>Ward 4 - <a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?abuttersDistance=200&amp;latlng=43.159995%2C-70.863065&amp;panel=themes&amp;previewId=I0002-G00000&amp;themes=%22%5B%5C%22wards-and-polling-places%5C%22%5D%22&amp;zoom=13" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Garrison School, 50 Garrison Road</a><br/>Ward 5 - <a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?abuttersDistance=200&amp;latlng=43.168732%2C-70.844285&amp;panel=themes&amp;previewId=H0011-001000&amp;themes=%22%5B%5C%22wards-and-polling-places%5C%22%5D%22&amp;zoom=13" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Dover Middle School, 16 Daley Drive</a><br/>Ward 6 - <a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?abuttersDistance=200&amp;latlng=43.231048%2C-70.916202&amp;panel=themes&amp;previewId=A0018-D00000&amp;themes=%22%5B%5C%22wards-and-polling-places%5C%22%5D%22&amp;zoom=13" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Hellenic Center, 219 Long Hill Road</a></p><p><a href="https://dovernh.mapgeo.io/datasets/properties?abuttersDistance=200&amp;latlng=43.187126%2C-70.890358&amp;panel=themes&amp;themes=%5B%22wards-and-polling-places%22%5D&amp;zoom=12"><em><strong>View an interactive Ward Map with Polling Places</strong></em></a></p><p>Voters may only vote in the ward in which they live.</p><p>Not sure of your polling location? Contact the City Clerk's Office at 603-516-6018.</p></div><h2>Absentee Ballots Now Available</h2><p>Absentee ballots are now available for Nov. 6, 2026 general election. </p><p>Per <a href="https://gc.nh.gov//rsa/html/LXIII/657/657-mrg.htm">state law</a>, any person who will be absent on the day of any state election because of a religious observance, physical disability and employment obligation (including care of children and infirm adults) may vote via absentee ballot. </p><p>A voter may also obtain an absentee ballot when the National Weather Service has issued a winter storm warning, blizzard warding, or ice storm warning for election day. </p><h3>How to obtain an absentee ballot</h3><p>A voter must complete an <a data-jcrpath="/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee Ballot Application.pdf" data-pathitem="{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;16777215-101-44565&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Absentee Ballot Application.pdf&quot;,&quot;folderPaths&quot;:[&quot;//Folders/$System$/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots&quot;],&quot;category&quot;:&quot;ASSET&quot;,&quot;revisionable&quot;:true,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;percFileAsset&quot;,&quot;leaf&quot;:true,&quot;hasItemChildren&quot;:false,&quot;hasFolderChildren&quot;:false,&quot;hasSectionChildren&quot;:false,&quot;mobilePreviewEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee Ballot Application.pdf&quot;,&quot;accessLevel&quot;:&quot;ADMIN&quot;,&quot;typeProperties&quot;:{&quot;entries&quot;:{}},&quot;folderPath&quot;:&quot;//Folders/$System$/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee Ballot Application.pdf&quot;,&quot;columnData&quot;:{}}" href="/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee%20Ballot%20Application.pdf" title="Absentee Ballot Request Form for Sept. 8, 2026 primary and Nov. 3, 2026 general elections">Absentee Ballot Application</a>, which declares the applicant a duly qualified voter of the city and the reason the voter is entitled to vote by absentee ballot. Applications are also available at the City Clerk's Office.</p><p>Deliver the completed <a data-jcrpath="/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee Ballot Application.pdf" data-pathitem="{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;16777215-101-44565&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Absentee Ballot Application.pdf&quot;,&quot;folderPaths&quot;:[&quot;//Folders/$System$/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots&quot;],&quot;category&quot;:&quot;ASSET&quot;,&quot;revisionable&quot;:true,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;percFileAsset&quot;,&quot;leaf&quot;:true,&quot;hasItemChildren&quot;:false,&quot;hasFolderChildren&quot;:false,&quot;hasSectionChildren&quot;:false,&quot;mobilePreviewEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee Ballot Application.pdf&quot;,&quot;accessLevel&quot;:&quot;ADMIN&quot;,&quot;typeProperties&quot;:{&quot;entries&quot;:{}},&quot;folderPath&quot;:&quot;//Folders/$System$/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee Ballot Application.pdf&quot;,&quot;columnData&quot;:{}}" href="/Assets/government/open-government/election-information/absentee-ballots/Absentee%20Ballot%20Application.pdf" title="Absentee Ballot Request Form for Sept. 8, 2026 primary and Nov. 3, 2026 general elections">Absentee Ballot Application</a> to the City Clerk's Office. It can be hand-delivered, mailed or faxed.</p><p><strong>City of Dover City Clerk's Office</strong><br/>288 Central Ave.<br/>Dover, NH 03820<br/>Phone 603-516-6018<br/>Fax: 603-516-6666<br/>Hours: Monday-Thursday, 8:30 a.m. to 5:30 p.m.; Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4 p.m.</p><h3>Deadline to return absentee ballots</h3><p><span>The deadline for returning absentee ballots to be counted in the general election:</span></p><ul><li><span><strong>In person</strong> — 5 p.m. Monday, Nov. 2, 2026, at the City Clerk's Office.</span></li><li><span><strong>By mail</strong> — 5 p.m. on Election Day, Tuesday, Nov. 3, 2026.</span></li></ul><h3>Absentee Ballot Status</h3><p><span>After you have applied for an absentee ballot, you can use the Secretary of State's</span> <a href="https://app.sos.nh.gov/">Voter Information Lookup</a><span> to find out if your clerk has received your request, when the absentee ballot was sent to you, and when your clerk received your completed absentee ballot.</span></p><hr/></div></div>
</div>
